        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0503" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v12/pg463"/>

                <head>201. Memorandum of a Conversation, Mid-Ocean Club, Bermuda, March 21, 1957, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d201-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">USDel/MC/2</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Tucker’s Town, Bermuda</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1957-03-21T20:00:00-04:00"
                            >March 21, 1957, 8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">United States</hi>
                        <list>
                            <item>Ambassador Whitney</item>
                            <item>Mr. Rountree</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">United Kingdom</hi>
                        <list>
                            <item>Prime Minister Macmillan</item>
                            <item>Mr. Selwyn Lloyd</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Baghdad Pact</item>
                </list>
                <p>At dinner with the Prime Minister and the Foreign Minister on March 21, I
                    informed them, in accordance with the Secretary’s instructions, that Ambassador
                    Richards had that day told the Turks that the United States would be willing to
                    join the Baghdad Pact Military Committee, if invited to do so by the members. I
                    read them the substance of Ambassador Richards’ telegram reporting his
                    conversation with the Turkish Prime Minister.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d201-f2"
                    /></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d201-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d201-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 62 D 181, CF 861. Secret.
                    Drafted by Rountree.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d201-f2" n="2" xml:id="d201-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d200"><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>.</p>
                <p>On March 22 during a news conference at Bermuda, Press Secretary Hagerty
                    announced that the United States through the Richards Mission had advised
                    members of the Baghdad Pact of its willingness to join the Military Committee of
                    the Pact. The text of Hagerty’s statement is printed in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >American Foreign Policy: Current Documents, 1957</hi>, p. 771.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
